Third-party material

The files wasm/cspice.wasm and wasm/cspice.mjs are compiled from the CSPICE
toolkit, which is produced by the Navigation and Ancillary Information Facility
(NAIF) at the Jet Propulsion Laboratory, California Institute of Technology, under
contract with NASA. The CSPICE source is obtained through the arturania/cspice
fork (https://github.com/arturania/cspice), which adds the Emscripten build
scripts, at the commit pinned in scripts/build-cspice.sh. CSPICE is distributed
under NAIF's own terms, not under the Apache License; see
https://naif.jpl.nasa.gov/naif/rules.html before redistributing.

The kernel fixtures under test/fixtures are bounded subsets of, or copies of,
public NAIF and PDS kernels (leapseconds, planetary constants, a de440s subset,
Cassini reconstructed ephemeris and instrument kernels, and the New Horizons MU69
low-polygon shape model), included only to make the tests deterministic.

